# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Value Council — data tree
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Local convention: ~/Library/Application Support/value-council/ is
# the canonical data root on Macs. The repo's data/ tree is what
# GitHub Actions writes into and commits back.
#
# Cache subtrees are intentionally never committed: they are large
# (~2GB), they are regenerable from public APIs, and committing them
# would inflate the repo to no benefit.
#
# One exception, and it is deliberate. company_names.json (~376K) is the
# ticker-to-company-name map every page renders, and the dashboard is
# now built in the cloud from this repo rather than served from the Mac.
# A build that cannot read it renders "AAPL" where "Apple Inc." belongs
# on every screen. It is regenerable but not from a build container, so
# it ships. The `data/cache/*` form is required over `data/cache/`:
# git does not descend into an excluded directory, so a negation inside
# one is never reached.
data/cache/*
!data/cache/company_names.json
data/fundamentals_cache/

