# macOS / iCloud name-collision duplicates.
#
# ~/Documents is under iCloud Drive sync, which resolves a collision by
# writing "name 2.ext" beside the original. Eighteen appeared during one
# working day, byte-identical to tracked files, and pytest collected the
# ten under tests/ — the suite read 1488 where the real figure is 1305.
# One of them was ".github/workflows/ci 2.yml", which would have run a
# second identical CI job on every push had it ever been committed.
#
# They are never wanted. Ignoring them keeps an accident out of history;
# deleting them is still a manual step, since ignoring only hides them.
# The pattern is literally "<name><space><digit>.<ext>". Anchoring on
# the space matters: a bare "*[0-9].py" would also swallow sp500.py.
* [0-9].py
* [0-9].yml
* [0-9].yaml
* [0-9].json
* [0-9].ts
* [0-9].tsx
* [0-9].md
* [0-9].toml
* [0-9].sqlite
* [0-9].plist
